/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (The project is an ESP32-based sensing system designed to detect human presence and movement using Wi-Fi signal variations. By analyzing changes in wireless signals within an environment, the system identifies human activity without relying on cameras or conventional motion sensors. It also visualizes these signal variations through a real-time thermal heatmap, where color intensity represents changes in signal strength and motion levels, providing a clear visual representation of human presence and movement.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
